Usage: watch [OPTION]... COMMAND

Execute a program periodically, showing output fullscreen.

Runs COMMAND repeatedly, displaying its output and errors.
This allows you to watch the program output change over time.

OPTIONS:
  -n, --interval NUM  seconds to wait between updates
  -d, --differences   highlight changes between updates
  -t, --no-title      turn off header showing interval and command
  -b, --beep          beep if command has a non-zero exit
  -c, --count NUM     number of times to run the command (for testing)
      --help          display this help and exit
  -V, --version       output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
